/**
 * @file 4Nodes.cnl
 * Test case for linNet.
 *
 * Four nodes and a branch in between all nodes to get a maximally complex
 * structure of the LES.
 *
 * A result check can be done by looking first at the dependency of Uout
 * only on U1 and then only on U2. For the dependency of Uout on U1, when
 * U2 is assumed zero, we can make these simplifications:
 *
 * - U1 shortcuts R5; R5 has no impact on the transfer function.
 * - U2 shortcuts R6; R6 has no impact.
 * - Node 2 becomes same as node gnd.
 * - R4 is parallel to R3; the pair can be replaced by R34=R3*R4/(R3+R4)
 * - R1 is parallel to R2; the pair can be replaced by R12=R1*R2/(R1+R2)
 * - U1 feeds a voltage divide of R34 and R12; Uout is the negative voltage at R12
 * - Uout=-R12/(R12+R34); this leads soon to linNets result:
 *
 *                       -(R1*R2*R3 + R1*R2*R4)
 * Uout(U1) = --------------------------------------------- * U1
 *             (R1*R2*R3 + R1*R2*R4 + R1*R3*R4 + R2*R3*R4)
 *
 * And analogously for Uout(U2).
 *
 * Copyright (C) 2013-2026 Peter Vranken (mailto:Peter_Vranken@Yahoo.de)
 *
 * This program is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify it
 * under the terms of the GNU General Public License as published by the
 * Free Software Foundation, either version 3 of the License, or (at your
 * option) any later version.
 *
 * This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but
 * WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of
 * MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE. See the GNU
 * General Public License for more details.
 *
 * You should have received a copy of the GNU General Public License along
 * with this program. If not, see <http://www.gnu.org/licenses/>.
 */

U U1  K3  K1
U U2  K2  gnd


R R3  \
  K3  \
  K2
R R2  K2  K1
R R6  K2  gnd
R R1  K1  gnd
R R5  K3  K1
R R4  K3  gnd

DEF   Uout K1 K2
RES   msResult Uout LIN 30 10. 10M
